CORE gcc-only
main.i
--arch x86_64
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
approximating inline assembly
--
The x86 inline assembly in main.c is interpreted exactly: if CBMC approximated
any statement (assigning nondeterministic values to its outputs), the
assertions, which check values observed on x86-64 hardware, would fail.
